{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782519589,"nonce":"IvrZG5AOTpw9CzacD5AaZJ5jdA0=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABG3lB3Q","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/337","origin":"github"},"title":"RCA: FCU 3D-gyro health failure on 2026-06-26 (gabby) — flag persists, data clean","message":"## Summary\n\nDuring the **2026-06-26 gabby/Lake Massabesic** deployment, the FCU reported a persistent **3D gyro health failure** (`mavros: System` = ERROR, \"Sensor health\"). The field session attributed two symptoms to it — full-throttle-on-manual and nav position/velocity jumps — and the fault survived a power cycle. Post-session bag analysis **confirms the gyro health bit is genuinely and persistently failed, but shows the published gyro *data* was clean**, which re-opens the cause of the full-throttle behavior. This issue tracks the FCU-side root-cause investigation.\n\n## Evidence (from session bags)\n\nSource: `~/data/logs/gabby/logs/bizzyboat/` (2026-06-26), topics `/diagnostics`, `/bizzy/mavros/imu/data`, independent `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu_data`.\n\n### 1. Isolated, persistent gyro health bit\n\nFCU SYS_STATUS, identical in every bag of the session:\n\n| Mask | Value |\n|------|-------|\n| Sensor present | `0x1230DC2B` |\n| Sensor enabled | `0x0220802B` |\n| Sensor health  | `0x0230812A` |\n\nDecoded: the **only** present+enabled sensor reporting unhealthy is **bit 0 = 3D_GYRO**. Accel, baro, GPS, motor outputs, AHRS, battery all healthy. Comm link clean (drop 0.0%, errors 0).\n\nThe field log's morning (`0x0230812A`) vs afternoon (`0x0230DD2A`) masks differ **only** in control-status bits (ANGULAR_RATE_CONTROL, ATTITUDE_STABILIZATION, YAW_POSITION, XY_POS_CONTROL) that come up on arm/controller-init — **not** the gyro bit. The power cycle did not clear the gyro.\n\n### 2. Gyro *data* was clean — flag, not corruption\n\nComparing the FCU gyro against the independent SBG INS gyro (rotation-invariant magnitude):\n\n| Bag (EDT) | FCU `mavros/imu/data` mean \\|ω\\| | SBG `sbg/imu_data` mean \\|ω\\| | NaNs |\n|-----------|----------------------------------|------------------------------|------|\n| 09:15 | 0.0139 rad/s | 0.0139 rad/s | 0 |\n| ~09:41 (at rest) | 0.0089 | 0.0090 | 0 |\n| 11:00 | 0.0155 | 0.0156 | 0 |\n\nThe FCU gyro stream had **0 NaNs, physically sane magnitudes, tracked real boat motion, and matched the independent SBG IMU to within noise**. A dead/stuck/garbage gyro would show NaNs, saturation, freezing, or divergence — none present. So **\"3D gyro = Fail\" is an FCU health/consistency flag, not visibly corrupt angular-rate data reaching autonomy.**\n\n## Implication for the full-throttle / nav-jump symptoms\n\nThe field theory was *bad gyro → EKF instability → nav jumps + full-throttle-on-manual*. The bag data **does not support the data-corruption link**: during the recorded window (which includes armed + GUIDED moments) the gyro data feeding the stack was clean. This re-opens the operator's original 10:16–10:18 suspects for full-throttle — the **GUIDED speed controller / setpoint path / FCU throttle params** (`CRUISE_THROTTLE` / `ATC_SPEED`) — rather than the gyro. The full-throttle behavior should be re-examined on the command/throttle side.\n\n## Caveats\n\n- **Afternoon symptom window not bagged.** Recording stops ~11:12 EDT; the post-reboot full-throttle-risk period (13:41 EDT+) was not captured, so gyro/nav behavior *during* the worst symptoms isn't directly observed.\n- **FCU mechanism not pinnable from ROS alone.** \"Gyro health fail\" with good data typically stems from a failed internal consistency/health check, gyro cal drift, or vibration/clipping — distinguishable only from the FCU dataflash, not the ROS bags.\n\n## Next diagnostic steps (FCU-side)\n\n1. Pull the ArduPilot dataflash `.bin` from the session — inspect `VIBE` (clip counts), `IMU` health, `ERR` / gyro-inconsistent events.\n2. Check `INS_GYR*` offsets / `INS_GYR_CAL`; try a stationary gyro recal and confirm whether the health bit clears.\n3. Verify IMU instance count — the present mask shows a single gyro instance (no GYRO2); confirm against the actual hardware (Cube/Pixhawk usually carries multiple IMUs).\n\n## Related\n\n- Field-import PR for the same session: #336 (Closes #335) — disabled `bathymetry_layer` (unrelated costmap-flood mitigation).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}